  "goodToKnow": "Der Feminismus is feminism; ironically for some, it's grammatically masculine, like all -ismus nouns. Der Feminist and die Feministin are feminists, and feministisch is the adjective. Alice Schwarzer founded the feminist magazine EMMA in 1977 and is one of Germany's best-known feminists. A lively German debate is about gendern, writing forms like Lehrer*innen to include all genders. Women in West Germany only got the right to work without their husband's permission in 1977."
